{"title":"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Guess_and_Check)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Guess and Check)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> a <i>7-10 double</i> if the digits of the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> form a base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> number that is twice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1fd7cb028e27b8648efbfb002f3e6d4fcb33a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$51$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is a 7-10 double because its base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> representation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419924dabadec1cbc40ad235df6230a545e2161f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$102$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. What is the largest 7-10 double?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610b3c7a96f222287cb81f761b0774b923e9faff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_7 = \\overline{a_na_{n-1}\\cdots a_0}_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />; we are given that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e28e31aaf18ab0eafe5466283a750f9e062edd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(a_na_{n-1}\\cdots a_0)_7 = (a_na_{n-1}\\cdots a_0)_{10}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" /> (This is because the digits in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> ' s base 7 representation make a number with the same digits in base 10 when multiplied by 2)\n</p><p>Expanding, we find that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c32c1f5624df09afd480557f3483b8f0ed4190.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\cdot 7^n a_n + 2 \\cdot 7^{n-1} a_{n-1} + \\cdots + 2a_0 = 10^na_n + 10^{n-1}a_{n-1} + \\cdots + a_0\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>or re-arranging,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/4574738c53d25fa109c96f5340f1e386649da59d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_0 + 4a_1 = 2a_2 + 314a_3 + \\cdots + (10^n - 2 \\cdot 7^n)a_n\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />s are base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fc5cafbb9898af4b423d18e85b46e2f97f6647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />, and the LHS is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Hence our number can have at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits in base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680402621fc353300ba9d680b956472fe8846b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011a9c93473ae33d92826a1626d38d2bb91b6d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$630_7 = \\boxed{315}_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\" /> is our largest 7-10 double.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Guess_and_Check.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Guess_and_Check)\">Solution 2 (Guess and Check)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Guess and Check)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> representation of our number, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be its base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> representation.\n</p><p>Given this is an AIME problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfcfea04dbe7e853fdbceac585084f66b16e2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. If we look at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, it must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b9116007a90d8b496b3a9aa7920304e0d94a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A$\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5590d5c8340b1bff9229a3b5320b3204d0aff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&lt;2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is looked at in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b833a70e5b34465a7e1cc445231d569f21b81da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f1ffc8a6829f25b0b0366087a70dfd4e06fef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as a number in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8de329c4f0f40890857c31bf4ee81771a20d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*7^3=686$\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce691b6538b3503b3539399a35513624ceb04e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$686$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is non-existent in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we're gonna have to bump that down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8adee99cf2cd5e83191257604ddefa083a991b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$666_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>This suggests that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94d79a7b67ccadbd1674c8661a23aa33a16b838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{666}{2}=333$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Guess and check shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9225b75c06b747eced0f754d2a0e08d8d18cbda0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&lt;320$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, and checking values in that range produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fda3881d5c613ddf53b52ec3486c4fbce890d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{315}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since this is an AIME problem, the maximum number of digits the 7-10 double can have is 3.  Let the number be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f86b25ae7388073d5246ea63f5f79fa8351738.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[abc\\]\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> in base 7. Then the number in expanded form is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea67b80166eac2f166da7b13faf695c4ab456da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[49a+7b+c\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" /> in base 7 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69de645547d0ad11136660dbebfe74745ecddbe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100a+10b+c\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> in base 10.  Since the number in base 7 is half the number in base 10, we get the following equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bfb804bb91db43473529d38492e39036a2f625.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[98a+14b+2c=100a+10b+c\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"14\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c5729c0b77257086eaf43990ed52e3adbb249e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a=4b+c.\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />  \nThe largest possible value of a is 6 because the number is in base 7.  Then to maximize the number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the largest 7-10 double is 630 in base 7, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fda3881d5c613ddf53b52ec3486c4fbce890d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{315}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> in base 10.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I\" title=\"2001 AIME I\">2001 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017115352\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 356/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9587/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.180      1 -total\n 57.83%    8.779      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.64%    6.017      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3061:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017115352 and revision id 206702. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}